# water_pool.tas — water from the fluid pass of the demo (REQ-VOXEL-028).
#
# Purpose: show the fluid stream of the mesh result and the fluid pass.
# With --place-block=water, hotbar slot 1 holds water. The player digs one
# ground block, places water in the hole, then places one more water cell
# on the grass next to the hole. The ray of the player goes through water.
#
# Scene (flatland, the same spawn each run): the player looks down about
# 30 degrees. The water in the hole has its surface below the grass (the
# fluid surface height is 0.875). The water cell on the grass shows its
# sides and its top surface, and the grass shows through the water.
#
# Usage (from the repo root):
#   zig build native -Dexample=voxel
#   ./zig-out/bin/voxel --world=flatland --aa=none --place-block=water \
#     --tas examples/voxel/tests/water_pool.tas \
#     --dump-frame=water_pool.ppm
#
# The golden `water_pool` of run_headless_regressions.sh is this frame.
#
# Tick numbering is relative to the first post-loading tick.

# --- Capture mouse ---
1 mouse_down left
2 mouse_up left

# --- Look down about 30 degrees (the same as hotbar_place.tas). ---
3 mouse_move 0 180

# --- Dig the ground block in front. ---
6 mouse_down left
7 mouse_up left

# --- Place water in the hole: the ray hits the top of the hole floor. ---
11 mouse_down right
12 mouse_up right

# --- Turn right a little, then place water on the grass. ---
16 mouse_move 220 0
20 mouse_down right
21 mouse_up right

# --- Turn back so the two water cells are in the frame. ---
25 mouse_move -110 -60

# --- Hold steady so --dump-frame lands on a stable view. ---
32 mouse_move 0 0
